{artist: Simon and Garfunkel }
{composer: Paul Simon }


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4fWyzwo1xg0   (Capo 4)

There's also an easier version to play which has an (Am) instead of the (Bm).

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  For the intro, form the modified (Bm) – a mini-barre on fret 2 with your ring and pinky on strings 3 and 4 of the 4th fret – leaving your middle finger hovering over the 2nd string/3rd fret.  Now pick the covered strings indicated and after the final 3-1 drop your middle finger onto the 2nd string/2nd fret and strum Bm on “Hello,”  For a different opening, hold the modified Bm formation and after the final 3-1 pick the 3rd string twice on “Hello”, then place that hovering middle finger down onto the open 2nd string/3rd fret and pick twice on “darkness” and the pick 1st string twice on “my old” and finish with a strum of (A) on “friend.”  After beginning the song play the (Bm) without the barre.

TIP:  Also notice there is a (D) to (Bm) to (D) sequence in the third and fourth lines of each verse.  From the (D) to (Bm) hold the (D) shape and add your pinky to the 3rd string/3rd fret to get to (Bm), and then lift off the pinky to return to the (D).  On/off.

TIP:  At the end of the song, after the final |Bm| lift off and “manually” pick the 2nd string/2nd fret <c#>, then the 2nd string/3rd fret <d>, and open 2nd string <b> -- do this twice -- and finish with single strum of |D|.  
  

